      "content": "but it's not just the fans. the fans are constant, they don't stutter like that. the stuttering only happens when the bandwidth usage hits a certain threshold on the monitored ports. it's too precise to be mechanical. it feels like i'm picking up the actual cadence of the handshakes or something. \n\nit just happened again. a very heavy, low thud, then three quick sharp clicks. like a heavy file being pushed through. does that sound like it could be encrypted traffic or maybe a specific handshake sequence? it feels way too rhythmic to be random hardware noise.",
